  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 145 AM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nIt still appears as though the high-amplitude/strong upper high will \nsubtly retrograde into the middle of the week, putting a check on \ntemperatures and keeping the door open for at least low \nprecipitation chances. \n\nThursday looks to be another \"cooler\" (yet still above average) day \non the temperature front, with upper-90s to near-100F highs across \nOklahoma and western-north Texas. The current forecast would \nadvertise the lowest/least areal coverage of heat headlines this \nday, though will be dependent on how surface features (namely a \nfront) evolves on Wednesday. It does currently appear that we begin \nto warm more notably into next weekend, as advection of warmer \nairmasses re-establishes. \n\nWhile no period stands out amongst the rest in terms of rain and \nstorm chances, our position relative to the aforementioned high will \nallow for at least episodic (low) chances from Thursday evening into \nthe weekend (especially across northern and western Oklahoma).\n\nUngar",
